<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AloneTogether-D-Theme" spTempo="120">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Alone Together

&quot;Alone Together&quot; is a song composed by
Arthur Schwartz with lyrics by Howard Dietz.
 It was introduced in the Broadway musical
Flying Colors in 1932 by Jean Sargent.

The song soon became a hit, with
Leo Reisman and His Orchestra&apos;s 1932
recording (vocal by Frank Luther)
being the first to reach the charts.

It has become a jazz standard. The first jazz
musician to record the song was Artie Shaw 
in 1939</spComments>
